<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss 1997 govt bonds to raise some 3.0 bln Sfr.</title>
<headline>Swiss 1997 govt bonds to raise some 3.0 bln Sfr.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss federal government plans to raise around 3.0 billion Swiss francs net and 4.5 billion francs gross via bond issues in 1997, the federal treasury in Berne said.  </p>
<p>It gave this schedule for emissions.</p>
<p>    Auction	Payment (prov)     Auction     Payment (prov)</p>
<p> 28 Nov 1996	13 Jan 97	   23 Jan 97    6 Feb 97</p>
<p> 27 Mar 97	  10 Apr 97	   22 May 97    5 Jun 97</p>
<p> 24 Jul 97	   7 Aug 97	   25 Sep 97    9 Oct 97</p>
<p> 27 Nov 97	   8 Jan 98</p>
<p>Called bonds (as of October 29, 1996):</p>
<p>Sfr 200 million 5.5 percent 90-8.01.99 called at par 8.1.97</p>
<p>Sfr 235 million 4.25 percent 89-11.1.01 Rep at 101 percent 11.1.97</p>
<p>The Swiss National Bank added in a statement that the government raised 2.8 billion francs net and 5.1 billion gross in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
